// ASYNC_PLAN.md §3.4: an `async_ngl bet` that fell over and that nobody ever
// awaited is an error thrown into the void, and the "no silent truncation"
// rule says it must not vanish. The program is told at exit, and the exit
// code says something went wrong.
//
// A *fulfilled* `otw` nobody awaited is deliberately not reported: starting
// work you do not need the answer to is a legitimate thing to do, and
// treating it as a fault would make fire-and-forget impossible.
//
// The detail goes in the diagnostic's roast rather than its message, because
// §4.2 renders the roast by default -- a report that said only "left on read"
// and left you to go looking would barely be a report.
async_ngl bet fine() {
    bounce "nobody needs this and that is fine"
}

async_ngl bet not_fine() {
    chuck oops("MathAintMathin", "nobody will ever know")
}

fine()
not_fine()
yap "the entry program finished normally"
